{"skill":{"slug":"clawdbot-filesystem","displayName":"Filesystem Management"},"version":{"version":"1.0.2","createdAt":1769481608074,"changelog":"Clean naming: Removed 'Clawdbot' from display name, fixed LICENSE.md extension","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"LICENSE.md","size":1074,"sha256":"ecab1e261aab2aa4dfa4d562c8e16b0be2ae34faea72d553a8980eb0b4ae9fef","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"README.md","size":9056,"sha256":"bd14e682785513a895cea184d12e75bdecbeb1d11d3b58742f6dfd73fe577349","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":6302,"sha256":"c36367f5492e8eec4c6e0d4a977a714786f72611f8d8ddd693aa0eaef2b07149","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"config.json","size":839,"sha256":"cd666d38f84b12ce5bac993b052c9a52ea7d270d0acb6b83705c733657e9aa18","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"package.json","size":1470,"sha256":"ef41ecff5b1c1539b74992b299bc9ab51ccc7735fe93930ea77bf8b9a6e2da20","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1785,"sha256":"445c6f123fd16e85108b73b6f9519a5915d1ad5ac34ad9b1ca9c528a681f683b","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789021712463,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"c4361cf7b6de39f0e132d75d755aa2ee712e1ba974ed441673d38059a7a8c59a","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/c4361cf7b6de39f0e132d75d755aa2ee712e1ba974ed441673d38059a7a8c59a","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: \nDeveloper: \nVersion: \nDescription: OpenClaw Agent Skill\n\nThe OpenClaw AgentSkills bundle 'clawdbot-filesystem' appears benign. Its stated purpose is advanced filesystem operations (list, search, copy, analyze), which aligns with the described functionality. Crucially, the `package.json` explicitly declares `network: \"none\"` and `system: \"none\"` permissions, and the `config.json` further restricts `allowedOperations` to `[\"read\", \"copy\", \"analyze\"]` while defining `protectedPaths` to prevent access to sensitive system directories. There is no evidence of prompt injection attempts in `SKILL.md` or `README.md` instructing the agent to perform unauthorized actions, exfiltrate data, or install backdoors. The `copy` operation, while a write action, is explicitly permitted and includes safety features like `--dry-run`.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160086092},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":12,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":4,"checkedAt":1789021712463},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This filesystem skill requests broad local file access, but its documented behavior is coherent with file listing, searching, analysis, and user-directed copying.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The manifest requests read-write filesystem permission and no network/system permission, which is proportionate for a filesystem management tool but inherently broad.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Installation instructions use normal ClawdHub, git clone, chmod, and optional npm global install/link flows; no hidden remote execution or persistence mechanism was found in the package artifacts.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The copy command can write files and optionally overwrite, and some live examples omit a nearby dry-run warning; however the write behavior is disclosed and directly related to the skill's purpose.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No cross-session hooks, background workers, credential use, memory writes, scheduled tasks, or privilege escalation behavior were found.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is advanced filesystem management, and the documented capabilities are file listing, content search, directory tree/statistics, and batch copy operations.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you want an agent-facing tool with read-write access to local files. Prefer dry runs before copy operations, verify destination paths carefully, and be cautious with --overwrite or broad recursive searches over private directories.","findings":"[SQP-2] expected: The documented copy command writes files and supports overwrite; this is expected for a batch copy feature, and the skill also documents dry-run, permission checks, backup prompts, and protected paths.\n[SQP-2] expected: The live copy example using --preserve could be clearer that it performs actual writes, but it is still a disclosed, user-directed filesystem operation rather than hidden mutation.\n[SQP-1] expected: The package description is broad, but it accurately describes a general filesystem utility and does not add unrelated authority or hidden behavior.\n[SQP-1] expected: Generic keywords such as files, directories, search, and automation may increase accidental routing risk, but they match the documented functionality and are not by themselves a security concern.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789021712463}}}}}